Block completing a Stage until the other party's Stages are reviewed and
taken in, and add `Stage.based_on`, in apps/api/docs/prototype/swagger.yaml

Generated on 2026-11-26, against the swagger.yaml committed in 7248bc2.
Apply from the repository root:

  git apply apps/api/docs/prototype/claude-exploration/swagger-review-rebase.patch

These come from the user's decisions on 2026-11-26, after reading the
data-sync slide (`data-sync-api-path.pdf`, cited as DSYNC p1):

1. `PUT …/stages/{stageid}` (`completeStage`) gets a blocking rule and a
   `422` response. The platform won't complete a Stage until every Stage
   another organisation has completed for the child has been reviewed
   (accepted or rejected) by this organisation and rebased in. The rule
   applies in both directions: Home YJS and caretaker.
2. `Stage` gets `based_on`: the `stageid` of the latest completed Stage
   this Stage has been rebased onto, rejected Stages included. Naming the
   latest one stands for every Stage before it, so the list doesn't grow
   with the child's history. The user chose this over the last 3 Stages
   or a version number for the child's list of Stages.
3. `PATCH …/stages/{stageid}` (`updateStage`) says to set `based_on` when
   rebasing.

The review itself stays as designed in option B1: `POST …/reviews` in
`claude-exploration/proposed-transfer-api.yaml`, with a reason from the
standard update list, which notifies the originator.

Not decided, and marked ⚠️ in the patch:

- the order of Stages, inferred to be by `completed_at`
- the `rule` ID that the new `422` returns, because no existing
  requirement covers this rule

Note that "rebase" now has two senses in this file: merging a stale push
of the same Stage (the concurrency model), and taking in another
organisation's completed Stage (this patch, and DSYNC).

